This project began as a fork of jev-router by Pratyush Garg
(https://github.com/gargpratyush/jev-router), used under the MIT License, and
has since developed independently.

What came from upstream: the idea of putting a local proxy in front of a
coding CLI, swapping the model on the way past, and asking TypeSafe Jev which
one to use. The first working versions of the Claude Code and Codex proxies
were theirs.

What was rewritten or added here:

  - Grok as a third supplier, including its model catalogue, config sentinel
    registration and cache handling.
  - Tiers as (model, effort) pairs rather than models alone, so the top tier
    is the strong model thinking longer rather than a costlier model.
  - Sub-agent routing across all three CLIs, each of which hides the fact
    somewhere different.
  - Length-hint stripping, so "answer in one sentence" cannot cost a tier.
  - Explicit-override detection anchored to model and tier names rather than
    to ordinary English.

Upstream continues separately and is not affiliated with this project.
